% Walkers: LCD L33791 and its Policy Article A52503 (DME MACs). A policy
% program of the DMEPOS model: it includes dmepos.le (orders, delivery,
% benefit category, continued need, refills) and states when a claim for a
% walker or a walker accessory is REASONABLE AND NECESSARY: the criteria 1–3
% of a standard walker (E0130, E0135, E0141, E0143) and its related
% accessories; the weight the heavy duty walkers (E0148, E0149) need; the
% restricted use of one hand the heavy duty, multiple braking system,
% variable wheel resistance walker (E0147) needs; the documented special
% features of the walker with trunk support (E0140); the height the leg
% extensions (E0158) need. The enclosed frame walker (E0144) is never
% covered ("the medical necessity ... has not been established"): no rule
% concludes it. The powered walker (E0152) and the combination wheeled walker
% with seat and transport chair (E0150) are not durable medical equipment
% (the Policy Article): they are in scope, and have no benefit category.
%
% How the criteria are read. The LCD's criteria are clinical findings about
% the beneficiary — a significant mobility limitation, that the beneficiary
% can safely use the walker, that a walker will sufficiently resolve the
% deficit, that a severe neurologic disorder or another condition restricting
% one hand precludes a standard walker, that the record justifies the special
% features of a trunk support walker — made by the treating practitioner and
% accepted or rejected on review: each is the judged template of dmepos.le,
% "the finding F about B is established" (or unsupported), with who found it
% and why. The findings this policy reads, and the criterion each stands for
% (the first is the finding pmd.le reads for the same criterion):
%   significant mobility limitation (1); walker can be safely used (2);
%   walker sufficiently resolves mobility deficit (3); standard walker
%   unusable due to restricted hand use (E0147: a severe neurologic disorder
%   or other condition causing the restricted use of one hand — obesity by
%   itself is not a reason); trunk support justified (E0140: the record
%   documents why the special features are medically necessary).
% What the record states as fact — the beneficiary's weight and height, that
% an accessory replaces a component of a beneficiary-owned walker, when the
% walker was first issued (its delivery date) — is a scenario fact. Six feet
% is read as 72 inches and one month as 30 days.
%
% Accessories. The LCD covers the "related accessories" of a covered walker
% under the walker's criteria; the Policy Article's coding guidelines say
% which codes are accessories of the initial issue (E0154, E0156, E0157,
% E0158) and which bill only replacements for covered, beneficiary-owned
% walkers (A4636, A4637, E0159), and that wheels (E0155) are either such a
% replacement or wheels added to a non-wheeled walker more than one month
% after its initial issue. Claims that do not meet the coding guidelines are
% denied as not reasonable and necessary (the LCD's "GENERAL" paragraph), so
% those restrictions are read here as criteria of the accessory's claim.
%
% The payment condition the policy adds (Policy Article A52503, "Policy
% specific information"): a claim for E0147 states the manufacturer's name
% and the product name/number. Not modelled: the KX/GA/GY/GZ modifiers (the
% supplier's record of the weight within one month of providing a heavy duty
% walker is the KX condition, not a coverage criterion), the PDAC coding
% verification of E0147, the Column I/Column II bundling of accessories
% billed with a walker, enhancement accessories (A9270) and gait trainer
% features (A9900), which are noncovered or not separately payable.

the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    % the record
    % candidate for dmepos.le (also a template of pmd.le and manual_wheelchairs.le)
    the weight of *a beneficiary* is *a number* pounds; undefined.
    the height of *a beneficiary* is *a number* inches; undefined.
    *an item* is a replacement for a component of *a device*; undefined.
    *a device* is owned by the beneficiary; undefined.
    *a claim* states the manufacturer name and product number of *an item*; undefined.
    % the codes
    code *a code* is excluded from the durable medical equipment benefit.
    % derived
    *an item* is a walker accessory.
    *an item* is a non-wheeled walker.
    *an item* must be identified by manufacturer and product on the claim.
    *a beneficiary* meets the criteria for a standard walker.
    *an item* meets the walker coverage criteria for *a beneficiary*.
    *a claim* meets the accessory specific criteria.

the knowledge base walkers includes these resources:
    dmepos.

the knowledge base walkers includes:

LCD L33791 is published at "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/lcd.aspx?lcdid=33791".
the text of LCD L33791 is at "sources/lcd/L33791.txt".
Policy Article A52503 is published at "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/article.aspx?articleid=52503".
the text of Policy Article A52503 is at "sources/article/A52503.txt".

% The walkers the Policy Article places outside the benefit.
code "E0152" is excluded from the durable medical equipment benefit,
    as stated in Policy Article A52503, confer "A powered walker (E0152) is noncovered as it does not meet the definition of DME".
code "E0150" is excluded from the durable medical equipment benefit,
    as stated in Policy Article A52503, confer "A combination wheeled walker with seat and transport chair (E0150) is noncovered as it does not meet the definition of DME".

% What a walker accessory is, and a non-wheeled walker (the Policy Article's
% coding guidelines).
rule walker_accessory with provenance Policy Article A52503,
        confer "Codes E0154, E0156, E0157, and E0158 can be used for accessories provided with the initial issue of a walker or for replacement components":
an item is a walker accessory
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["E0154", "E0155", "E0156", "E0157", "E0158", "E0159", "A4636", "A4637"].

rule non_wheeled_walker with provenance Policy Article A52503,
        confer "when wheels are subsequently added to a covered, beneficiary-owned nonwheeled walker (E0130, E0135)":
an item is a non-wheeled walker
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["E0130", "E0135"].

% The one code whose claim must name the manufacturer and the product.
rule walker_identified_product with provenance Policy Article A52503,
        confer "When code E0147 is billed, the claim must include the manufacturer’s name and product name/number":
an item must be identified by manufacturer and product on the claim
    if the HCPCS code of the item is "E0147".

section applicability is:

% The codes this policy decides, and their benefit: durable medical equipment
% (Policy Article A52503), except the two walkers that are not DME.
rule walkers_codes with provenance Policy Article A52503,
        confer "Walkers are covered under the Durable Medical Equipment benefit":
the policy for code a code is walkers
    if the code is in ["E0130", "E0135", "E0140", "E0141", "E0143", "E0144", "E0147", "E0148", "E0149", "E0150", "E0152", "E0154", "E0155", "E0156", "E0157", "E0158", "E0159", "A4636", "A4637"].

rule walkers_benefit with provenance Policy Article A52503,
        confer "Walkers are covered under the Durable Medical Equipment benefit":
the benefit category of code a code is durable medical equipment
    if the policy for code the code is walkers
    and it is not the case that
        code the code is excluded from the durable medical equipment benefit.

section question is:

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% A walker: the criteria of its kind.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

rule walkers_walker with provenance LCD L33791,
        confer "A standard walker (E0130, E0135, E0141, E0143) and related accessories are covered if all of the following criteria (1-3) are met":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the item meets the walker coverage criteria for the beneficiary.

% Criteria 1–3: the findings of the treating practitioner.
rule walkers_criteria_1_to_3 with provenance LCD L33791,
        confer "The beneficiary has a mobility limitation that significantly impairs his/her ability to participate in one or more mobility-related activities of daily living (MRADL) in the home":
a beneficiary meets the criteria for a standard walker
    if the finding significant mobility limitation about the beneficiary is established
    and the finding walker can be safely used about the beneficiary is established
    and the finding walker sufficiently resolves mobility deficit about the beneficiary is established.

rule walkers_standard with provenance LCD L33791,
        confer "A standard walker (E0130, E0135, E0141, E0143) and related accessories are covered if all of the following criteria (1-3) are met":
an item meets the walker coverage criteria for a beneficiary
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["E0130", "E0135", "E0141", "E0143"]
    and the beneficiary meets the criteria for a standard walker.

rule walkers_heavy_duty with provenance LCD L33791,
        confer "A heavy duty walker (E0148, E0149) is covered for beneficiaries who meet coverage criteria for a standard walker and who weigh more than 300 pounds":
an item meets the walker coverage criteria for a beneficiary
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["E0148", "E0149"]
    and the beneficiary meets the criteria for a standard walker
    and the weight of the beneficiary is a number pounds
    and the number > 300.

rule walkers_multiple_braking with provenance LCD L33791,
        confer "A heavy duty, multiple braking system, variable wheel resistance walker (E0147) is covered for beneficiaries who meet coverage criteria for a standard walker and who are unable to use a standard walker due to a severe neurologic disorder or other condition causing the restricted use of one hand":
an item meets the walker coverage criteria for a beneficiary
    if the HCPCS code of the item is "E0147"
    and the beneficiary meets the criteria for a standard walker
    and the finding standard walker unusable due to restricted hand use about the beneficiary is established.

% An enclosed frame walker (E0144) is never covered: "The medical necessity
% for a walker with an enclosed frame (E0144) has not been established." No
% rule concludes it.

rule walkers_trunk_support with provenance LCD L33791,
        confer "A walker with trunk support (E0140) is covered for beneficiaries who meet coverage criteria for a standard walker and who have documentation in the medical record justifying the medical necessity for the special features":
an item meets the walker coverage criteria for a beneficiary
    if the HCPCS code of the item is "E0140"
    and the beneficiary meets the criteria for a standard walker
    and the finding trunk support justified about the beneficiary is established.

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% Accessories: covered under the walker's criteria, with the code's own
% conditions.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

rule walkers_accessories with provenance LCD L33791,
        confer "A standard walker (E0130, E0135, E0141, E0143) and related accessories are covered if all of the following criteria (1-3) are met":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the item is a walker accessory
    and the item is an accessory of a device
    and the device is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the device meets the walker coverage criteria for the beneficiary
    and the claim meets the accessory specific criteria.

rule walkers_initial_accessories with provenance Policy Article A52503,
        confer "Codes E0154, E0156, E0157, and E0158 can be used for accessories provided with the initial issue of a walker or for replacement components":
a claim meets the accessory specific criteria
    if the claim is for an item
    and the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["E0154", "E0156", "E0157"].

% six feet is 72 inches
rule walkers_leg_extensions with provenance LCD L33791,
        confer "Leg extensions (E0158) are covered only for beneficiaries 6 feet tall or more":
a claim meets the accessory specific criteria
    if the claim is for an item
    and the HCPCS code of the item is "E0158"
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the height of the beneficiary is a number inches
    and the number >= 72.

rule walkers_replacement_accessories with provenance Policy Article A52503,
        confer "Codes A4636, A4637, and E0159 are only used to bill for replacement items for covered, beneficiary-owned walkers":
a claim meets the accessory specific criteria
    if the claim is for an item
    and the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["A4636", "A4637", "E0159"]
    and the item is a replacement for a component of a device
    and the device is owned by the beneficiary.

rule walkers_replacement_wheels with provenance Policy Article A52503,
        confer "Code E0155 can be used for replacements on covered, beneficiary-owned wheeled walkers":
a claim meets the accessory specific criteria
    if the claim is for an item
    and the HCPCS code of the item is "E0155"
    and the item is a replacement for a component of a device
    and the device is owned by the beneficiary.

% wheels added to a non-wheeled walker more than one month (30 days) after
% its initial issue, which is its delivery
rule walkers_added_wheels with provenance Policy Article A52503,
        confer "Code E0155 cannot be used for wheels provided at the time of, or within one month of, the initial issue of a non-wheeled walker":
a claim meets the accessory specific criteria
    if the claim is for an item
    and the HCPCS code of the item is "E0155"
    and the item is an accessory of a device
    and the device is a non-wheeled walker
    and the device is owned by the beneficiary
    and the device was delivered on a date
    and the date of service of the claim is an other date
    and the other date is a number days after the date
    and the number > 30.

section remedy is:

% The policy's own condition of payment: the E0147 claim names the product.
rule walkers_documentation_e0147 with provenance Policy Article A52503,
        confer "When code E0147 is billed, the claim must include the manufacturer’s name and product name/number":
the policy specific documentation requirements are met for a claim
    if the policy of the claim is walkers
    and the claim is for an item
    and the item must be identified by manufacturer and product on the claim
    and the claim states the manufacturer name and product number of the item.

rule walkers_documentation_others with provenance Policy Article A52503,
        confer "When code E0147 is billed, the claim must include the manufacturer’s name and product name/number":
the policy specific documentation requirements are met for a claim
    if the policy of the claim is walkers
    and the claim is for an item
    and it is not the case that
        the item must be identified by manufacturer and product on the claim.
